  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1240 PM MDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nConditions will remain pretty consistent Thursday through Saturday. \nHighs will be warm, in the low-mid 80s over the plains and in the \n70s over the valleys. Afternoon showers and storms will mainly be \nover the La Garitas and parts of the central mountains on Thursday, \nwith coverage being much more isolated on Friday. Moisture starts to \nincrease on Saturday, with showers and storms possible over a good \nportion of our western mountains, though coverage still looks \nscattered at best. \n\nSunday and onwards, activity will start to increase as a pair of \ndeepening upper lows set up, one over the Pacific Northwest and \nanother SW of the California coastline. Flow aloft will turn more \nsouthwesterly as well, funneling more moisture into the mountains. \n\nBeyond that, model solutions really start to vary as we head into \nnext week, with a wide range of different solutions for the path, \nspeed, amplitude, and evolution of the upper-level pattern. General \nconfidence is that next week will be noticeably cooler and wetter \nacross the region, but specific impacts will need more time to come \ninto focus amongst the model solutions.",
